 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508082,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A  person who weighs 200 pounds on Earth would weigh only 33 pounds on the moon. A 2021 Toyota Prius weighs 3,040 pounds on Earth; how much would it weigh on the moon? Round to the nearest tenth if necessary.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Set up the two ratios as proportions.</p>\n<p>Let <i>x</i> = weight on the moon.</p>\n<p>It helps many students to create a table to help set up their ratios.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Conversion</td>\n<td>What I have or want</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Weight on Earth</td>\n<td>200</td>\n<td>3,040</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Weight on the moon</td>\n<td>33</td>\n<td><i>x</i></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Set up your proportion.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{200}}{{33}} = \\frac{{3,040}}{x}\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"200x = \\left( {33} \\right)\\left( {3,040} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Cross multiply.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"200x = 100,320\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{200x}}{{200}} = \\frac{{100,320}}{{200}}\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x = 501.6\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The weight of the car on Mars is exactly 501.6 pounds.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "501.6 pounds"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
